---
/* HOW COMPLETE «WHO TO CONTACT» IS, SAID IN NUMBERS. The Atlas means to be the place somebody looks first; a reader (and the next harvest)
   can only trust that if the gaps are printed beside what is held. Read from public/contacts/coverage.json, which scripts/contacts/build.py
   counts from the same rows the pages show. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import coverage from "../../public/contacts/coverage.json";
import registry from "../../../data/contacts/sources.json";

const SAY = { "town-hall": "Town halls", church: "Parishes and places of worship", diocese: "Dioceses and church archives", cemetery: "Burial grounds",
  "cemetery-manager": "Cemetery managers", archive: "Archives", library: "Libraries", museum: "Museums and memorials", university: "Universities",
  society: "Societies and volunteers", other: "Others" };
/* Kinds the Atlas has no list of its own for: «known» is only what a contact source has named, so a share would flatter. */
const NO_LIST = new Set(["town-hall", "cemetery-manager", "museum", "university"]);
const n = (v) => v.toLocaleString("en");
const share = (c) => {
  if (NO_LIST.has(c.kind)) return "not counted yet";
  const pc = 100 * c.reach / c.known;
  return pc > 0 && pc < 0.1 ? "under 0.1%" : `${pc.toFixed(pc < 10 && pc > 0 ? 1 : 0)}%`;
};
const countries = new Intl.DisplayNames(["en"], { type: "region" });
---
<Base title="Who to contact: how complete it is" description="How many archives, parishes, burial grounds, libraries and town halls Record Atlas knows, and how many of them it can tell you how to reach.">
  <p class="cap">Each place page lists the contacts held within 20 km. This is how far that goes today. «Can be written to or rung» means an e-mail, telephone,
  postal address or contact form; a website alone is counted apart. Entries are joined only where two sources share an exact identifier, so one ground listed
  by two sources can count twice.</p>
  <div style="overflow-x:auto">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Known</th><th>Can be written to or rung</th><th>Share</th><th>With e-mail</th><th>Website only</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {coverage.kinds.map((c) => (
          <tr><td>{SAY[c.kind] || c.kind}</td><td>{n(c.known)}</td><td>{n(c.reach)}</td><td>{share(c)}</td><td>{n(c.email)}</td><td>{n(c.webOnly)}</td></tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <h2>Where there is no contact</h2>
  <p>A place page or a map dot suggests the town hall or the diocese whose boundary holds the spot, and says that it is a suggestion: the details are
  that office's own, never the burial ground's or the parish's. Nothing is suggested by nearness, and suggestions are not counted above.
  {coverage.areas.countries.length ? `So far: ${n(coverage.areas["town-hall"])} municipalities and ${n(coverage.areas.diocese)} dioceses, in ${coverage.areas.countries.map((cc) => countries.of(cc)).join(", ")}.` : "No boundaries are held yet."}</p>
  <h2>Where the contacts come from</h2>
  <ul>
    {Object.entries(registry.sources).map(([id, s]) => (
      <li><a href={s.url}>{s.title}</a>: {s.licence}. {n(coverage.rows[id] || 0)} rows{coverage.harvested[id] ? `; harvested country by country, so far ${coverage.harvested[id].map((cc) => countries.of(cc)).join(", ")}` : ""}.</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  <p>Only organisations' own mailboxes are kept; an address that names a person is left out, and a free-mail address is kept only where it names the
  institution. No contact is guessed from a parent body or a homepage.
  The files are open: see <a href={u("/data/")}>the data page</a>.</p>
</Base>
